From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fardjad Davari <public@fardjad.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 14:50:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: enforce ordered web-search engine policy

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: Make web-search engine selection an ordered,
configuration-owned allowlist with scalar compatibility.
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: personal-feature
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: 1020-personal-feature-make-completion-quality-gates-respect-review-setti.patch

Patch intent:
Treat [websearch].engine as the complete ordered engine policy. Accept the
legacy scalar and canonical array forms, normalize aliases and duplicates, and
attempt configured engines in priority order only.

Why it exists:
A web-search tool request could previously select an engine outside the
configured policy, including DuckDuckGo when SearXNG was explicitly selected.
This patch removes engine selection from the public schema, rejects a legacy
request for a non-primary engine, preserves legacy fallback migration, and
makes list and scalar environment overrides explicit. It does not add new
search providers or change result parsing.

Upstream integration points:
crates/jcode-config-types/src/lib.rs owns WebSearchConfig deserialization,
defaults, aliases, and serialization. crates/jcode-base/src/config/
config_file.rs and env_overrides.rs load and validate TOML and environment
policy. The websearch tool in crates/jcode-app-core/src/tool/websearch.rs
dispatches the normalized list and retains legacy request decoding for
in-flight callers. README.md and the default config template document the
policy and overrides.

Update guidance:
Preserve scalar compatibility and the default DuckDuckGo-then-Bing order while
keeping the normalized engine vector as both allowlist and priority. If the
legacy fallback key is removed, migrate its documented behavior deliberately.
Any new dispatch path must consume the normalized list and must not reintroduce
request-level engine selection or bypass strict environment validation.

Validation:
scripts/isolate_config.py -- cargo test -p jcode-config-types websearch_config_tests --lib
scripts/isolate_config.py -- cargo test -p jcode-app-core tool::websearch::tests --lib
scripts/isolate_config.py -- cargo test -p jcode-base websearch_ --lib
